<clickhouse>
    <!-- Several tests in this module assert the legacy behavior of a cluster without an interserver
         <secret>: the initiator forwards the initiating user (initial_user) to the shard over an
         unauthenticated connection, and the shard uses it for currentUser(), row policies and
         system.user_query_log. Since the forged-initial-user fix this is off by default (the shard
         uses the authenticated connection user, so a client cannot impersonate anyone), and this
         setting opts back into the legacy, insecure behavior so those tests keep exercising it.
         The default-secure behavior is covered by
         tests/queries/0_stateless/05616_forged_secondary_query_identity. -->
    <trust_initial_user_without_interserver_secret>true</trust_initial_user_without_interserver_secret>
</clickhouse>
